  { q: 'Why did Apollo turn the raven black?', a: 'According to Ovid, Apollo was furious at the raven for delivering the news of Coronis\'s infidelity — not at Coronis herself. He scorched the raven\'s plumage black in his anger. This is counterintuitive (the raven was delivering true information) and the myth is often read as a warning: do not be the bearer of bad news, or more specifically, do not gossip.' },
